WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.100
-In yet another sign

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.200
that the Republican Party

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.934
has been fully captured
by Trumpism,

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.400
the GOP is rallying behind

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.601
several pro-Trump
Senate candidates

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.367
whose campaigns have been
engulfed in scandal,

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:13.434
as Trump himself continues
to face more legal scrutiny

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.133
over the stolen
classified documents

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.467
he stashed away at Mar-A-Lago.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.567
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:22.634
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.667
President Biden was
in Florida yesterday

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.067
to survey hurricane damage,

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.934
where he delivered
a very heartfelt speech

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.968
about unity
and putting politics aside

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.734
to help the people affected
by the storm.

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.801
Although, at one point,
Biden did find a way

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.200
to sneak in a little jab

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.701
at Florida
Governor Ron DeSantis,

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.000
by praising him for something,
I'm guessing,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.501
DeSantis does not want
to be praised for.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:00.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.667
-It's a pretty slick move

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.601
[ Laughter ]
to congratulate
a political opponent

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:07.701
for a thing they don't want
to be congratulated for,

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.801
in a situation
where they can't respond.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.434
[ As Biden ]
Yeah, he told me that
this morning,

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:14.133
while we were eating
our vegan breakfast burritos.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:15.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:18.033
He also told me he's happy
Velma's gay now.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.434
Such a crafty old-man move,

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.334
to undercut someone
by complimenting them.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.367
It's like your grandpa
giving you credit

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.467
for putting your phone down
during Thanksgiving.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:29.067
[ Garrulous voice ]
I know, if I'm thankful
for anything,

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.634
it's that Timmy decided to join
us here in the real world.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.734
You know, we really appreciate

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:35.701
you taking time out of your busy
schedule there, bud.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.934
We know how hard you work,
watching those TikToks.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.300
But the real attention grabbing
moment yesterday

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.033
was actually caught
on a hot mic

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:46.868
when Biden was talking to the
mayor of Fort Myers Beach,

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.234
Ray Murphy, and said this --

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.767 --> 00:01:59.834
-Whoa!

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:00.634
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.267
That escalated very fast.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:05.167
So, he went from Uncle Joe

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:07.534
to Scranton Joe
in like a heartbeat.

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:08.667
[ Laughter ]
He's like --

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.167
[ As Biden ]
God bless you and keep you.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.234
"Thank you, sir."

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.801
And thank the good people
of Fort Myers

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:13.934
for all their strength
and courage.

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:14.734
"Well, yes, sir."

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.567
And just remember

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.834
what my grandma always said --

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:19.467
"[Bleep] around and find out."

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
My question is

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.567
what were they talking about?

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:24.033
How did that even come up?

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:26.968
Also, when I first heard it,
I thought,

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:29.100
"Is the mayor also a Biden?"

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.133
[ Laughter ]
But he's not.

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.200
He's a Murphy.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.701
Because when I use the phrase
a Meyers,

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:35.400
I tend to be talking
to other Meyers.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.601
Like when I pull my kids
in close and say,

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.734
"No one picks a Meyers first
for dodgeball!"

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.968
[ Laughter ]
Which is fair.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:45.067
We're just genetically bad
at dodging.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.434
But, of course,
it will not surprise you

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:49.033
to learn that right-wing pundits
did not like this.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.100
After four years
of nonstop politeness

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.334
from President Wallflower
over here,

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:56.033
[ Laughter ]
they were absolutely shocked

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.400
to hear profanity,
although, one host,

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.167
in particular,
accidentally made Biden

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.868
look even cooler
with his graphics.

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:02.267
-Joe Biden was in Florida today,

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:04.033
blaming hurricanes
on global warming.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.868
If only we give him control
of the weather, he'd fix it.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:09.501
While down there,
he was caught on a hot mic,

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.267
warning his enemies.

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.701
[ Laughter ]
Alright, tough guy!

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.801
He's going to put a severed
horse head in your bed,

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.000
if you don't stop
asking questions.

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:20.033
Pathetic.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.667
[ Laughter ]
-Is it, pathetic?

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.534
Because your graphic makes him
look [bleep] awesome.

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.334
[ As Biden ]
I came here to eat ice cream
and kick ass,

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.634
and this ice cream's
melting real fast.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:32.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.467
It looks like the poster
for an action movie

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.367
where Biden is played
by Jason Statham.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:38.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.434
So, while Biden was in Florida,
he may have dropped

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.467
some soft burns
and occasional profanity,

00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:44.634
but, otherwise, he stayed
above the fray of politics,

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:47.868
even as the midterms intensify,
with less than five weeks to go.

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:50.234
Now, obviously, the midterms
are deeply consequential,

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.734
for both his presidency

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.234
and for the future
of our democracy.

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:55.501
Republicans have nominated
pro-Trump election deniers

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.300
up and down the ballot
across the country

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.634
and, while the opposition
party historically

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.167
is always heavily favored

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.067
to perform well
in off-year elections,

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.868
Republicans are stumbling
toward the finish line

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:07.434
after several of their
pro-Trump, MAGA candidates

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:08.567
have just fully imploded.

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.868
A MAGA candidate
in a swing district in Ohio

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.601
reportedly lied
about his military service;

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.767
Pennsylvania Senate candidate
Dr. Oz

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.567
has been accused
of killing over 300 dogs

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:18.701
in his scientific experiments;

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.801
and Georgia state candidate
Herschel Walker,

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.434
who favors a ban on abortion,

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:24.634
is dealing with the fallout
from the bombshell allegation

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:26.868
that he paid
for a girlfriend's abortion.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.601
Among many other shocking
revelations that should,

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.667
in a healthy democracy,
be disqualifying,

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:33.167
the craziest thing, to me,
is the GOP

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.033
just never runs
out of ways to shock you.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.367
The Democrats, no doubt,
have their flaws,

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:39.300
but the GOP is like a magnet

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.901
for all these pathological liars
with incredibly sordid pasts.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.133
I can't even begin to imagine

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.934
who Trump is going
to endorse next.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.634
[ As Trump ]
You know, I was watching
"House of the Dragon"

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:49.534
and I thought,
"I like this Daemon guy."

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:51.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
I like him a lot.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.601
Bad wig, great guy, big sword.

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:53.734
We need more swords.

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.400
We need more swords in D.C.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.133
With all these crooked Dems
running around, we need a sword.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:00.100
And I said, "Daemon,
before I endorse you,

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.033
is there anything I should know?

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.868
Is there anything I should know
about you, Daemon,

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.033
that might get me in trouble?"

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.534
And he said,
"I am both married to

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:07.734
and sleeping with my niece."

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.400
[ Laughter ]
And I said,

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.801
I said, "I don't think that's
going to be a problem."

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:14.334
[ Laughter and applause ]
Walker,

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:16.434
in particular,
was hand-picked by Trump,

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:18.667
despite repeated warnings
about his troubled past,

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:20.901
but it seems like
that might actually be

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:22.767
what attracted Trump to him
because, according

00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:24.701
to New York Times reporter
Maggie Haberman,

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:27.667
who'd just written a 600-page
tell-all about Trump,

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:31.167
he actually enjoys
degrading our institutions,

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.367
bringing out the worst
in people,

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.167
and proving that there is
no rock bottom.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:37.300
There's no bare minimum level
of decency required

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.634
of public figures anymore.

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:41.701
-Does he want
the Herschel Walkers to win,

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.067
to prove this point?

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:45.767
Does he want more damage
to Republicans in the party?

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:48.200
-He wants to show
that nothing matters

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.167
and one of his goals --
and I write about this --

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:53.367
is he believes that everyone
is just like him.

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:54.868
Everything is a transaction.

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:56.334
Everything can be exchanged.

00:05:56.334 --> 00:05:58.000
Everything can be reduced
to a deal.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.567
There are no red lines.

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.534
And so, to show
that there are no red lines

00:06:01.534 --> 00:06:02.968
always makes him happy.

00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:04.634
-I honestly didn't think
there was anything

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:06.133
that made Trump happy,
but now we know

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:08.634
there is one thing --
making the rest of us miserable.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.267
Like his mood will never change,

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:12.367
but if he brings our moods
down enough,

00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:14.567
his sour existence will count
as happy

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:16.534
and then, I don't know,
he'll get a morning show

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:18.601
where they spell his name
with an exclamation point?

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:20.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.067 --> 00:06:22.901
And you can tell Trump delights
in blowing through red lines

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:25.000
because he does it all the time
and keeps doing it,

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.033
even now that he's no longer
in office

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:29.167
and facing multiple serious
criminal investigations.

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:32.334
For example, most people
would shy away from the cameras,

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:34.133
if they were
under federal investigation

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:36.501
for stealing highly classified
documents from the White House,

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:39.400
but, in a speech this week,
Trump actually bragged

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.300
that the FBI search
of Mar-A-Lago

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.000
gave him free publicity.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.634
-You probably read and heard
about the document hoax.

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:48.501
Has anyone heard
about the document hoax,

00:06:48.501 --> 00:06:50.968
helicopters flying
over Mar-A-Lago?

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:52.767
[ Murmuring ]
Well, they've given us

00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:55.634
about $5 billion worth
of free publicity, I will say.

00:06:55.634 --> 00:06:57.601
People say,
"That's a nice house."

00:06:57.601 --> 00:06:59.067
[ Laughter ]
If it weren't so nice,

00:06:59.067 --> 00:07:00.834
they probably wouldn't be
doing it.

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:02.133
Because, you know,
it gets ratings.

00:07:02.133 --> 00:07:04.534
When they look, they say,
"That's a beautiful place."

00:07:04.534 --> 00:07:07.033
-Maybe the search got publicity
for Mar-A-Lago,

00:07:07.033 --> 00:07:08.801
but I don't think
it's good publicity.

00:07:08.801 --> 00:07:11.667
I've never walk by a hotel
surrounded by cop cars

00:07:11.667 --> 00:07:13.300
and circling helicopters
and thought,

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.033
"Ooh!
That looks like a fun place

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:17.133
[ Laughter ]
for a little rest
and relaxation.

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:18.834
Let me look it up on Yelp."

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:23.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:23.834 --> 00:07:25.334
"I like those odds!"

00:07:25.334 --> 00:07:27.968
But then Trump made it
even weirder when he managed

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:30.601
to pull everyone in the audience
into his mess with him.

00:07:30.601 --> 00:07:33.200
-No other president
has been harassed

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:36.567
and persecuted like we have.

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:38.534
I speak on behalf of you, too.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:39.567
-[ Laughing ]
On behalf of you, too?

00:07:39.567 --> 00:07:40.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.734 --> 00:07:42.133
[ As Trump ]
They're harassing all of us

00:07:42.133 --> 00:07:45.367
because we all still those
classified documents together.

00:07:45.367 --> 00:07:47.868
[ Laughter ]
I'm including you guys.
You were there, too.

00:07:47.868 --> 00:07:49.801
You said, "Donald,
take the nuclear blueprints,"

00:07:49.801 --> 00:07:51.133
and I said,
"Are you sure this is legal?"

00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:52.467
And you guys were like,
"Yeah, go for it."

00:07:52.467 --> 00:07:54.300
And I said, "Okay."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.167
But only because you,
the audience,

00:07:56.167 --> 00:07:57.634
this audience, told me to.

00:07:57.634 --> 00:07:58.934
It was your idea, not mine.

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:01.267
We all remember it.
We all remember it.

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:02.934
You said, "Do it."
I said, "Maybe not,"

00:08:02.934 --> 00:08:05.033
and then you pressured me.
You bullied me.

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:06.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.634 --> 00:08:08.734
So, FBI, if you're listening,
you'd better bring

00:08:08.734 --> 00:08:10.267
a whole lot of handcuffs.

00:08:10.267 --> 00:08:11.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.434 --> 00:08:13.367
So, Trump wants to prove
that nothing matters,

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:15.534
that there's no bar anymore
for public decency,

00:08:15.534 --> 00:08:17.067
that everyone is just
as bad as him.

00:08:17.067 --> 00:08:18.634
The problem is,
for most of us, he's wrong.

00:08:18.634 --> 00:08:20.701
There are still red lines.

00:08:20.701 --> 00:08:22.834
I mean, let's remember,
this guy has been rejected

00:08:22.834 --> 00:08:24.534
over and over
by a majority of voters.

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:27.300
He only fell ass-backwards
into the presidency the one time

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:30.000
because we have an insane system
where the loser gets the job.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.567
I have a feeling,
if the framers had been capable

00:08:32.567 --> 00:08:34.367
of imagining Trump at the time,

00:08:34.367 --> 00:08:36.934
they definitely would've bailed
on the Electoral College.

00:08:36.934 --> 00:08:39.067
Like if Trump had existed
in the 1700s,

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:41.133
you know, in those tights,
a powdered wig,

00:08:41.133 --> 00:08:43.167
tricorner hat,
just downing gallons

00:08:43.167 --> 00:08:44.367
of Ye Olde Diet Coke,

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:46.400
[ Laughter ]
selling scam products like,

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.300
I don't know...

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:49.501
[ Laughter ]
or whatever,

00:08:49.501 --> 00:08:51.367
insulting beloved
American politicians,

00:08:51.367 --> 00:08:53.133
the framers would've come up
with a better system.

00:08:53.133 --> 00:08:54.767
[ As Trump ]
George Washington, he's a loser.

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.234
Have you seen his boat?
So small.

00:08:56.234 --> 00:08:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.667 --> 00:08:59.300
It can only fit like nine guys,

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.234
not even enough room
for him to sit down.

00:09:01.234 --> 00:09:03.133
He has to stand in the front
like a dog.

00:09:03.133 --> 00:09:06.400
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.901
Like if the founding fathers
had come up

00:09:07.901 --> 00:09:10.567
with the Electoral College
and then they met Trump,

00:09:10.567 --> 00:09:13.501
they would've been like,
"Oh, [bleeping].

00:09:13.501 --> 00:09:14.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.033
Quick, somebody invent Wite-Out.

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.167
We got to undo this."

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:18.067
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:19.267
The point is, Trump is wrong.

00:09:19.267 --> 00:09:20.968
Most people
do still have red lines

00:09:20.968 --> 00:09:22.567
and that's why
they've rejected him

00:09:22.567 --> 00:09:23.767
over and over at the polls.

00:09:23.767 --> 00:09:26.234
Trump has exposed the GOP
as morally bankrupt,

00:09:26.234 --> 00:09:27.434
over and over and over,

00:09:27.434 --> 00:09:29.400
and now it's happening,
yet again, as they rally

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.667
around various Senate candidates
engulfed in scandal.

00:09:31.667 --> 00:09:34.567
There is simply no lie
too bald-faced for Trump.

00:09:34.567 --> 00:09:36.701
He'll say anything.
If he thought he would get away

00:09:36.701 --> 00:09:38.434
with it, he'd tell people
he was best friends

00:09:38.434 --> 00:09:40.133
with Bono and the Edge
and say --

00:09:40.133 --> 00:09:42.033
-I speak on behalf of U2.

00:09:42.033 --> 00:09:45.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:46.767 --> 00:09:48.567
[ Cheering and applause ]
-No. I'm not okay with that.

00:09:48.567 --> 00:09:49.667
I'm not okay with it.

00:09:49.667 --> 00:09:51.601
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:51.601 --> 00:09:54.767
♪♪

00:09:54.767 --> 00:09:56.567
The midterm elections
are coming up, so,

00:09:56.567 --> 00:09:59.167
to make sure that you're good
to vote in this election,

00:09:59.167 --> 00:10:02.234
visit our good friends
at headcount.org

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:06.300
to check your voter registration
status or to register to vote.

